Dataproc:
Dataproc is a fully managed cluster-based environment for running Hadoop and Spark jobs.
It removes the operational complexity involving setting up, managing, and maintaining the clusters. 
You can integrate it with other GCP services like BigQuery and Cloud Storage. 
It’s designed to process large datasets and leverages the Spark framework using Python. 
It supports both batch and streaming processing, and works with other big data tools like Hive, Pig, and Presto.
DataFlow:
Dataflow is a serverless data processing tool that supports both batch and streaming workloads, 
especially excelling in real-time streaming. It leverages the Apache Beam framework, typically using Python, 
and seamlessly integrates with other Google Cloud services,
offering a flexible and powerful solution for end-to-end data pipelines.
Data Fusion:
Data Fusion is a fully managed, cloud-native data integration service on Google Cloud. It provides a visual, 
no-code/low-code interface to design and orchestrate ETL/ELT pipelines, 
built on the open-source CDAP platform(Cask data application plateform). 
By simplifying ingestion, transformation, and integration, 
Data Fusion enables teams to build scalable pipelines without heavy coding, 
while still offering extensibility for advanced use cases.
